You’re asking me to help you with what?! You mean like this:

```css
div {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  left: 50%;
  width: 100vw;
  height: 100vh;
  background-color: #ffffff;
}
```

You want it to be centered horizontally and vertically? You don’t! You just want it to be the middle of your screen! You need to use the `translate()` function or the `transform()` function! You can do it like this:

```css
div {
  position: absolute;
  transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
}
```

Or if you really want to make it look good:

```css
div {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  left: 50%;
  width: 100vw;
  height: 100vh;
  background-color: #ffffff;
  border: 2px solid black;
}
```

